WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.329
As Edward walked away from the palace, people continued to laugh whenever he called himself a prince.

2
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:13.150
He continued to shout at them for not recognizing him as the heir to the throne.

3
00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:20.202
At last everyone got bored and ignored him.

4
00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:26.767
By this time Edward's feet were sore, so he stopped to bathe them in a creek.

5
00:00:26.768 --> 00:00:30.810
Looking around, he recognized a nearby building.

6
00:00:30.811 --> 00:00:35.976
His father had turned it into a home for poor, abandoned children.

7
00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:40.699
"My father has been generous to the children," Edward thought.

8
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.873
"So I'll be treated kindly there."

9
00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:50.636
He looked down at his ragged clothes, which belonged to Tom, and sighed.

10
00:00:50.637 --> 00:00:56.683
"Right now I'm as poor as the children who live there."

11
00:00:56.684 --> 00:01:00.457
Edward spotted a group of boys playing in a courtyard.

12
00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:04.220
They were all dressed alike in the school's uniform.

13
00:01:04.221 --> 00:01:10.210
The boys quickly gathered around Edward, who misinterpreted this as a sign of respect.

14
00:01:10.211 --> 00:01:20.295
"Good lads," he said, "please tell whoever is in charge of this home that Prince Edward wishes to speak to him."

15
00:01:20.296 --> 00:01:28.979
A loud shout went up, and the boys laughed at this stranger in rags.

16
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:35.041
"And who are you, beggar?" asked one boy, who seemed to be their leader.

17
00:01:35.042 --> 00:01:39.714
"The prince's messenger?"

18
00:01:39.715 --> 00:01:44.241
"I am the prince! How dare you speak to me that way!"

19
00:01:44.242 --> 00:01:49.924
Edward was outraged because he was used to being obeyed, not insulted.

20
00:01:49.925 --> 00:01:56.064
His hand flew to his hip, but he found nothing there.

21
00:01:56.065 --> 00:01:59.433
"Did you see that?" another boy asked.

22
00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:06.407
"He thought he had a sword just like a real prince!"

23
00:02:06.408 --> 00:02:08.569
The boys laughed again.

24
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.590
Edward stood up tall.

25
00:02:10.591 --> 00:02:16.061
"You should be grateful that my father, the king, provides you with food and clothing.

26
00:02:16.062 --> 00:02:19.363
And you shouldn't be rude to me."

27
00:02:19.364 --> 00:02:28.284
This made the boys laugh even louder.

28
00:02:28.285 --> 00:02:32.931
"You are correct, Your Royal Highness," the first boy said.

29
00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:36.741
"Down on your knees, loyal subjects!"

30
00:02:36.742 --> 00:02:42.822
Snickering and poking each other, the boys dropped to their knees and bowed their heads.

31
00:02:42.823 --> 00:02:46.551
Tired of being mocked, Edward kicked at the nearest boy.

32
00:02:46.552 --> 00:02:50.863
"Take that!" he cried as he missed.

33
00:02:50.864 --> 00:02:53.963
The group's mood instantly changed to anger.

34
00:02:53.964 --> 00:02:58.035
"Throw him in the creek!" someone called out.

35
00:02:58.036 --> 00:03:01.992
For a moment Edward was stunned.

36
00:03:01.993 --> 00:03:05.123
These boys were going to toss him in the water!

37
00:03:05.124 --> 00:03:08.584
Then he turned and ran as fast as he could.

38
00:03:08.585 --> 00:03:12.647
He didn't dare look back until he was far away. When

39
00:03:12.648 --> 00:03:18.414
he did, the boys were nowhere to be seen. "It's

40
00:03:18.415 --> 00:03:24.130
a good thing I'm a fast runner." Edward smiled in spite of himself. "I

41
00:03:24.131 --> 00:03:30.215
could probably beat Tom Canty and his friends." For

42
00:03:30.216 --> 00:03:35.903
the rest of the day, Edward wandered the streets, looking for Tom's house. "If

43
00:03:35.904 --> 00:03:42.514
I can find Offal Street, Tom's family will realize that I'm the prince," he thought. "And

44
00:03:42.515 --> 00:03:48.446
they'll immediately take me back to the palace." But

45
00:03:48.447 --> 00:03:52.868
as night fell, Edward was still out on the streets. He

46
00:03:52.869 --> 00:03:56.978
grew so tired and hungry that he could barely walk. He

47
00:03:56.979 --> 00:04:05.802
gave up asking for directions because everyone insulted him instead of helping him. After

48
00:04:05.803 --> 00:04:10.600
a while he stopped being angry with the boys at the children's home. "Food

49
00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:16.068
and clothing are important, but they're not enough," he thought. "When

50
00:04:16.069 --> 00:04:20.991
I'm king, those boys will have an education too. And

51
00:04:20.992 --> 00:04:25.751
hopefully, they'll learn to be kind." Edward

52
00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:31.310
pressed on as it began to rain and the wind picked up. He

53
00:04:31.311 --> 00:04:36.290
drifted deeper into the maze of filthy streets where the poor lived. Suddenly

54
00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:40.572
a man grabbed Edward by the back of his neck. "Got

55
00:04:40.573 --> 00:04:42.919
you!" he cried. "Out

56
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:48.121
at this time of night, and I bet you don't have a penny to bring home. If

57
00:04:48.122 --> 00:04:52.204
that's not true, then my name's not John Canty, and I'll—" "John

58
00:04:52.205 --> 00:04:57.784
Canty?" Edward twisted around to see the man's face. "Are

59
00:04:57.785 --> 00:05:00.260
you really John Canty? Then

60
00:05:00.261 --> 00:05:05.748
you must be his father! Take me back to the palace immediately." "

61
00:05:05.749 --> 00:05:08.977
His father? The palace?

62
00:05:08.978 --> 00:05:11.488
I don't know what you're talking about.

63
00:05:11.489 --> 00:05:15.836
But I do know that I'm your father, and you'll soon regret—"

64
00:05:15.837 --> 00:05:20.080
"I can't stand this a minute longer!" Edward cried.

65
00:05:20.081 --> 00:05:26.057
"Take me back to my father, King Henry, and he'll make you rich beyond your wildest dreams.

66
00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:29.409
Believe me, I'm telling the truth.

67
00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:37.450
I am Prince Edward, the heir to the throne. I'm not Tom!"

68
00:05:37.451 --> 00:05:40.966
Confused, John stared at the boy.

69
00:05:40.967 --> 00:05:45.978
"I don't know what game you're playing, or if there's something wrong with your mind.

70
00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:52.657
But you're going home with me to Offal Street." He grabbed Edward again.

71
00:05:52.658 --> 00:05:57.161
"Help me!" Edward cried as people passed by.

72
00:05:57.162 --> 00:06:04.445
But John was already dragging the frantic, struggling boy toward Offal Street.

73
00:06:04.446 --> 00:06:13.368
A few curious onlookers followed them, but no one tried to help poor Edward.

